G2532.b:
⟪καί⟫, conj., ⟪and⟫.
⟪I.⟫ Copulative.
	⟪1.⟫ Connecting single words;
		⟪(a)⟫ in general: ⟦Matthew 2:18|Mt 2:18⟧ ⟦Matthew 16:1|16:1⟧, ⟦Mark 2:15|Mk 2:15⟧, ⟦Luke 8:15|Lk 8:15⟧, ⟦Hebrews 1:1|He 1:1⟧, al. mult.; repeated before each of the terms in a series, ⟦Matthew 23:23|Mt 23:23⟧, ⟦Luke 14:21|Lk 14:21⟧, ⟦Romans 7:12|Ro 7:12⟧ ⟦Romans 9:4|9:4⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ connecting numerals (WM, § 37, 4): ⟦John 2:20|Jo 2:20⟧, ⟦Acts 13:20|Ac 13:20⟧;
		⟪(c)⟫ joining terms which are not mutually exclusive, as the part with the whole: ⟦Matthew 8:33|Mt 8:33⟧ ⟦Matthew 26:59|26:59⟧, ⟦Mark 16:17|Mk 16:17⟧, ⟦Acts 5:29|Ac 5:29⟧, al.
	⟪2.⟫ Connecting clauses and sentences: ⟦Matthew 3:12|Mt 3:12⟧, ⟦Acts 5:21|Ac 5:21⟧, al. mult.; esp.
		⟪(a)⟫ where, after the simplicity of the popular language, sentences are paratactically joined (WM, § 60, 3; M, Pr., 12; Deiss., LAE, 128 ff.): ⟦Matthew 1:21|Mt 1:21⟧ ⟦Matthew 7:25|7:25⟧, ⟦Mark 9:5|Mk 9:5⟧, ⟦John 10:3|Jo 10:3⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ joining affirmative to negative sentences: ⟦Luke 3:14|Lk 3:14⟧, ⟦John 4:11|Jo 4:11⟧, ⟦3 John 1:10|III Jo 10⟧;
		⟪(c)⟫ consecutive, ⟪and so⟫: ⟦Matthew 5:15|Mt 5:15⟧ ⟦Matthew 23:32|23:32⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:19|He 3:19⟧, al.; after imperatives, ⟦Matthew 4:19|Mt 4:19⟧, ⟦Luke 7:7|Lk 7:7⟧, al.;
		⟪(d)⟫ = καίτοι, ⟪and yet⟫: ⟦Matthew 3:14|Mt 3:14⟧ ⟦Matthew 6:26|6:26⟧, ⟦Mark 12:12|Mk 12:12⟧, ⟦Luke 18:7|Lk 18:7⟧ (Field, Notes, 72), ⟦1 Corinthians 5:2|I Co 5:2⟧, al.;
		⟪(e)⟫ beginning an apodosis (= Heb. ⁨וְ⁩; so sometimes δέ in cl.), ⟪then⟫: ⟦Luke 2:21|Lk 2:21⟧ ⟦Luke 7:12|7:12⟧, ⟦Acts 1:10|Ac 1:10⟧; beginning a question (WM, § 53, 3a): ⟦Mark 10:26|Mk 10:26⟧, ⟦Luke 10:29|Lk 10:29⟧, ⟦John 9:36|Jo 9:36⟧.
	⟪3.⟫ Epexegetic, ⟪and⟫, ⟪and indeed⟫, ⟪namely⟫ (WM, § 53, 3c): ⟦Luke 3:18|Lk 3:18⟧, ⟦John 1:16|Jo 1:16⟧, ⟦Acts 23:6|Ac 23:6⟧, ⟦Romans 1:5|Ro 1:5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:5|I Co 3:5⟧, al.
	⟪4.⟫ In transition: ⟦Matthew 4:23|Mt 4:23⟧, ⟦Mark 5:1|Mk 5:1⟧, ⟦Mark 5:21|21⟧, ⟦John 1:19|Jo 1:19⟧, al.; so, Hebraistically, καὶ ἐγένετο (⁨וַיְהִי⁩; also ἐγένετο δέ), ⟦Mark 1:9|Mk 1:9⟧ (cf. ⟦Luke 5:1|Lk 5:1⟧; V. Burton, §§ 357-60; M, Pr., 14, 16).
	⟪5.⟫ καὶ . . . καί, ⟪both . . . and⟫ (for τε . . . καί, v.s. τε);
		⟪(a)⟫ connecting single words: ⟦Matthew 10:28|Mt 10:28⟧, ⟦Mark 4:41|Mk 4:41⟧, ⟦Romans 11:33|Ro 11:33⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ clauses and sentences: ⟦Mark 9:13|Mk 9:13⟧, ⟦John 7:28|Jo 7:28⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:22|I Co 1:22⟧, al.
⟪II.⟫ Adjunctive, ⟪also⟫, ⟪even⟫, ⟪still⟫: ⟦Matthew 5:39|Mt 5:39⟧, ⟦Matthew 5:40|40⟧, ⟦Mark 2:28|Mk 2:28⟧, al. mult.; esp. c. pron., adv., etc., ⟦Matthew 20:4|Mt 20:4⟧, ⟦John 7:47|Jo 7:47⟧, al; ὡς κ., ⟦Acts 11:17|Ac 11:17⟧; καθὼς κ., ⟦Romans 15:7|Ro 15:7⟧; οὕτω κ., ⟦Romans 6:11|Ro 6:11⟧; διὸ κ., ⟦Luke 1:35|Lk 1:35⟧; ὁ κ. (Deiss., BS, 313ff.), ⟦Acts 13:9|Ac 13:9⟧; pleonastically, μετὰ κ.. (Bl., §77, 7; Deiss., BS, 265 f,), ⟦Philippians 4:3|Phl 4:3⟧; τί κ., ⟦1 Corinthians 15:29|1 Co 15:29⟧; ἀλλὰ κ., ⟦Luke 14:22|Lk 14:22⟧, ⟦John 5:18|Jo 5:18⟧, al.; καίγε (M, Pr., 230; Burton, § 437), ⟦Acts 17:27|Ac 17:27⟧; καίπερ, ⟦Hebrews 5:8|He 5:8⟧; κ. ἐάν, v.s. ἐάν.

G2536.b:
⟪Καινάμ⟫ (T, Καϊ-; Rec. Καϊνάν), ό, indecl. (Heb. ⁨קֵינָן⁩), ⟪Cainam⟫, ⟪Cainan⟫;
⟪1.⟫ son of Enos (⟦Genesis 5:9|Ge 5:9⟧): ⟦Luke 3:37|Lk 3:37⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Son of Arphaxad (⟦Genesis 10:24|Ge 10:24⟧(LXX): ⟦Luke 3:36|Lk 3:36⟧.†

G2542.b:
⟪Καισαρία⟫ (Rec. -άρεια), -ας, ἡ, ⟪Cæsarea⟫;
⟪1.⟫ ⟪Cæsarea Philippi⟫, at the foot of Lebanon: ⟦Matthew 16:13|Mt 16:13⟧, ⟦Mark 8:27|Mk 8:27⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪Cæsarea⟫ of Palestine, on the sea-coast: ⟦Acts 8:40|Ac 8:40⟧ ⟦Acts 9:30|9:30⟧ ⟦Acts 10:1|10:1⟧, ⟦Acts 10:24|24⟧ ⟦Acts 11:11|11:11⟧ ⟦Acts 12:19|12:19⟧ ⟦Acts 18:22|18:22⟧ ⟦Acts 21:8|21:8⟧, ⟦Acts 21:16|16⟧ ⟦Acts 23:23|23:23⟧, ⟦Acts 23:33|33⟧ ⟦Acts 25:1|25:1⟧, ⟦Acts 25:4|4⟧, ⟦Acts 25:6|6⟧, ⟦Acts 25:13|13⟧.†

G2560.b:
⟪κακῶς⟫
(< κακός), adv.,
[in LXX: Wi 18:19, IV Mac 6:17, al.; κ. εἰπεῖν, ἐρεῖν (⁨ארר⁩, ⁨קלל⁩ pi.), ⟦Exodus 22:28|Ex 22:28⟧(⟦Exodus 22:27|27⟧), ⟦Leviticus 19:14|Le 19:14⟧, ⟦Isaiah 8:21|Is 8:21⟧; κ. ἔχειν (⁨חלה⁩, ⟦Ezekiel 34:4|Ez 34:4⟧, al.;] ⟪badly⟫, ⟪ill⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ in physical sense: κ. ἔχειν, ⟪to be ill⟫, ⟦Matthew 4:24|Mt 4:24⟧ ⟦Matthew 8:16|8:16⟧ ⟦Matthew 9:12|9:12⟧ ⟦Matthew 14:35|14:35⟧ ⟦Matthew 17:15|17:15⟧, ⟦Mark 1:32|Mk 1:32⟧, ⟦Mark 1:34|34⟧ ⟦Mark 2:17|2:17⟧ ⟦Mark 6:55|6:55⟧, ⟦Luke 5:31|Lk 5:31⟧ ⟦Luke 7:2|7:2⟧; πάσχειν, ⟦Matthew 17:15|Mt 17:15⟧ (WH, mg.); δαιμονίζεσθαι, ⟦Matthew 15:22|Mt 15:22⟧; κακοὺς κ. ἀπολέσει (as freq. in cl., v. LS, s.v.; MM, Exp., xv), ⟪evil that they are⟫, ⟪he will evilly⟫, etc., ⟦Matthew 21:41|Mt 21:41⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ in moral sense, ⟪wrongly⟫ (I Mac 7:42, IV Mac 6:17, al.): κ. λαλεῖν, ⟦John 18:23|Jo 18:23⟧; εἰπεῖν, c. acc. pers., ⟦Acts 23:5|Ac 23:5⟧; αἰτεῖσθαι, ⟦James 4:8|Ja 4:8⟧.†

G2563.b:
⟪κάλαμος⟫, -ου, ὁ,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨קָנֶה⁩, ⟦Isaiah 42:3|Is 42:3⟧, ⟦Ezekiel 40:3|Ez 40:3⟧ ff., al.;] ⟪a reed⟫: ⟦Matthew 11:7|Mt 11:7⟧ ⟦Matthew 12:20|12:20⟧(LXX), ⟦Luke 7:24|Lk 7:24⟧; hence, acc. to its various uses,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a reed-pipe⟫, ⟪flute⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪a reed-staff⟫, ⟪staff⟫ (cf. ⟦2 Kings 18:21|IV Ki 18:21⟧, ῥάβδος καλαμίνη): ⟦Matthew 27:29|Mt 27:29⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:30|30⟧, ⟦Matthew 27:48|48⟧, ⟦Mark 15:19|Mk 15:19⟧, ⟦Mark 15:36|36⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪a measuring reed⟫ or ⟪rod⟫ (⟦Ezekiel 40:3|Ez 40:3⟧ ff.): ⟦Revelation 11:1|Re 11:1⟧ ⟦Revelation 21:15|21:15⟧, ⟦Revelation 21:16|16⟧;
⟪(d)⟫ ⟪a writing reed⟫, ⟪a pen⟫: ⟦3 John 1:13|III Jo 13⟧ (cf. Milligan, NTD, 9, 7).†

G2596.b:
⟪κατά⟫ (bef. a vowel κατ’, καθ’; on the freq. neglect of elision, v. Tdf., Pr., 95; WH, App., 146a), prep. c. gen., acc., ⟪down⟫, ⟪downwards⟫.
⟪I.⟫ C. gen. (WM, § 47, k; Bl., § 42, 2).
	⟪1.⟫ C. gen. rei, in local sense;
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪down⟫, ⟪down from⟫: ⟦Matthew 8:32|Mt 8:32⟧, ⟦Mark 5:13|Mk 5:13⟧, ⟦Luke 8:33|Lk 8:33⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 11:4|I Co 11:4⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ ⟪throughout⟫ (late usage; Bl., § 42, 2): κ. ὅλης κ.τ.λ., ⟦Luke 4:14|Lk 4:14⟧ ⟦Luke 23:5|23:5⟧, ⟦Acts 9:31|Ac 9:31⟧ ⟦Acts 10:37|10:37⟧;
		⟪(c)⟫ in a peculiar adjectival phrase: ἡ κ. βάθους πτωχεία, deep or extreme poverty, ⟦2 Corinthians 8:2|II Co 8:2⟧.
	⟪2.⟫ C. gen. pers., usually in hostile sense;
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪against⟫ (in cl. only after verbs of speaking, witnessing, etc.): opp. to ὑπέρ, ⟦Mark 9:40|Mk 9:40⟧; μετά, ⟦Matthew 12:30|Mt 12:30⟧; after ἐπιθυμεῖν, ⟦Galatians 5:17|Ga 5:17⟧; λαλεῖν, ⟦Acts 6:13|Ac 6:13⟧; διδάσκειν, ⟦Acts 21:28|Ac 21:28⟧; ψεύδεσθαι, ⟦James 3:14|Ja 3:14⟧; after verbs of accusing, etc., ⟦Matthew 5:23|Mt 5:23⟧, ⟦Luke 23:14|Lk 23:14⟧, ⟦Romans 8:33|Ro 8:33⟧, al.; verbs of fighting, prevailing, etc., ⟦Matthew 10:35|Mt 10:35⟧, ⟦Acts 14:2|Ac 14:2⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 4:6|I Co 4:6⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ of swearing, ⟪by⟫: ὄμνυμι κ. (Bl., § 34, 1), ⟦Hebrews 6:13|He 6:13⟧, ⟦Hebrews 6:16|16⟧, cf. ⟦Matthew 26:63|Mt 26:63⟧.
⟪II.⟫ C. acc. (WM, § 49 d; Bl., § 42, 2).
	⟪1.⟫ Of motion or direction;
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪through⟫, ⟪throughout⟫: ⟦Luke 8:39|Lk 8:39⟧ ⟦Luke 9:6|9:6⟧ ⟦Luke 10:4|10:4⟧, ⟦Acts 8:1|Ac 8:1⟧, ⟦Acts 8:36|36⟧, al.;
		⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to⟫, ⟪towards⟫, ⟪over against⟫: ⟦Luke 10:32|Lk 10:32⟧ (Field, Notes, 62), ⟦Acts 2:10|Ac 2:10⟧ ⟦Acts 16:7|16:7⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:11|Ga 2:11⟧, ⟦Philippians 3:14|Phl 3:14⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ in adverbial phrases, ⟪at⟫, ⟪in⟫, ⟪by⟫, ⟪of⟫: κατ’ οἶκον, ⟪at home⟫, ⟦Acts 2:46|Ac 2:46⟧; κατ’ ἰδίαν (v.s. ἴδιος); καθ’ ἑαυτόν, ⟦Acts 28:16|Ac 28:16⟧, ⟦Romans 14:22|Ro 14:22⟧, ⟦James 2:17|Ja 2:17⟧; c. pron. pers., ⟦Acts 17:28|Ac 17:28⟧ ⟦Acts 18:15|18:15⟧, ⟦Romans 1:15|Ro 1:15⟧, ⟦Ephesians 1:15|Eph 1:15⟧, al.
	⟪2.⟫ Of time, ⟪at⟫, ⟪during⟫, ⟪about⟫: ⟦Acts 8:26|Ac 8:26⟧ ⟦Acts 12:1|12:1⟧ ⟦Acts 19:23|19:23⟧, ⟦Romans 9:9|Ro 9:9⟧, ⟦Hebrews 1:10|He 1:10⟧, al.
	⟪3.⟫ Distributive;
		⟪(a)⟫ of place: κ. τόποὐς, ⟦Matthew 24:7|Mt 24:7⟧, al.; κ. πόλιν, ⟦Luke 8:1|Lk 8:1⟧, ⟦Luke 8:4|4⟧, al.; κ. ἐκκλησίαν, ⟦Acts 14:23|Ac 14:23⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ of time: κ. ἔτος, ⟦Luke 2:41|Lk 2:41⟧; ἑορτήν, ⟦Matthew 27:15|Mt 27:15⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ of numbers, etc.: καθ’ ἕνα πάντες, ⟦1 Corinthians 14:31|I Co 14:31⟧ (on καθ’ εἷς, v.s. εἷς); κ. ἑκατόν, ⟦Mark 6:40|Mk 6:40⟧; κ. μέρος, ⟦Hebrews 9:5|He 9:5⟧; κ. ὄνομα, ⟦John 10:3|Jo 10:3⟧.
	⟪4.⟫ Of fitness, reference, conformity, etc.;
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪in relation to⟫, ⟪concerning⟫: ⟦Romans 1:3|Ro 1:3⟧, ⟦Romans 1:4|4⟧ ⟦Romans 7:22|7:22⟧ ⟦Romans 9:3|9:3⟧, ⟦Romans 9:5|5⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:26|I Co 1:26⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 10:18|10:18⟧, ⟦Philippians 1:12|Phl 1:12⟧; κ. πάντα, ⟦Acts 17:22|Ac 17:22⟧, ⟦Colossians 3:20|Col 3:20⟧, ⟦Colossians 3:22|22⟧, ⟦Hebrews 2:17|He 2:17⟧ ⟦Hebrews 4:15|4:15⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ ⟪according to⟫, ⟪after⟫, ⟪like⟫: ⟦Mark 7:5|Mk 7:5⟧, ⟦Luke 2:27|Lk 2:27⟧, ⟦Luke 2:29|29⟧, ⟦John 7:24|Jo 7:24⟧, ⟦Romans 8:4|Ro 8:4⟧ ⟦Romans 14:15|14:15⟧, ⟦Ephesians 2:2|Eph 2:2⟧, ⟦Colossians 2:8|Col 2:8⟧, ⟦James 2:8|Ja 2:8⟧, al.
⟪III.⟫ In composition, κ. denotes,
	⟪1.⟫ ⟪down⟫, ⟪down from⟫ (καταβαίνω, etc.), hence, metaph.;
		⟪(a)⟫ victory or rule over (καταδουλόω, -κυριεύω, etc.);
		⟪(b)⟫ "perfective" action (M, Pr., 111 ff.).
	⟪2.⟫ ⟪under⟫ (κατακαλύπτω, etc.).
	⟪3.⟫ ⟪in succession⟫ (καθεξῆς).
	⟪4.⟫ ⟪after⟫, ⟪behind⟫ (καταλείπω).
	⟪5.⟫ Hostility, ⟪against⟫ (καταλαλέω).
